0f6443238260a"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"D, 20 square units","reason":"AD=AP+PD=5, and all rhombus sides are equal, so AB=5. In right triangle APB, BP=sqrt(5²-3²)=4. Therefore the rhombus has area AD×BP=5×4=20.","status":"matches"},"assessed":true,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_p147"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2022_AMC_10B_Q02","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_189","cnm_075"],"id":"base-and-perpendicular-height","label":"Find the height using the right triangle","methodDirectNodeIds":{"base-and-perpendicular-height":["cnm_174","cnm_p147"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_174","cnm_p147","cnm_189","cnm_075"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":4,"alignmentIds":["alignment:06d5a7e54bf0f6443238260a"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"C, 7.6","reason":"The rectangle has area 10·8=80. The four corner triangles total 2(4·3/2)+2(6·5/2)=42, leaving parallelogram area 38. Since HE=√(4²+3²)=5, its corresponding height is d=38/5=7.6.","status":"matches"},"assessed":true,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_p147"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2004_AMC_8_Q24","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"parallelogram-area-and-height","label":"Find area, then divide by the base","methodDirectNodeIds":{"parallelogram-area-and-height":["cnm_p150","cnm_p089","cnm_p148","cnm_174","cnm_p147"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_p150","cnm_p089","cnm_p148","cnm_174","cnm_p147"]},{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_p077","cnm_p105","cnm_p103","cnm_075"],"id":"area-and-height","label":"Find the area, then the height","methodDirectNodeIds":{"area-and-height":["cnm_p147","cnm_p150","cnm_p089","cnm_p148","cnm_174"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_p147","cnm_p150","cnm_p089","cnm_p148","cnm_174","cnm_p077","cnm_p105","cnm_p103","cnm_075"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":4,"alignmentIds":["alignment:06d5a7e54bf0f6443238260a"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"D, 20","reason":"AD=AP+PD=5, and the rhombus gives AB=5. Since BP is perpendicular to AD, BP=√(5²-3²)=4. Therefore the area is AD×BP=5×4=20.","status":"matches"},"assessed":true,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_p147"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2022_AMC_12B_Q02","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_189","cnm_p105","cnm_075"],"id":"method_1","label":"Base and perpendicular height","methodDirectNodeIds":{"method_1":["cnm_p147","cnm_174"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_p147","cnm_174","cnm_189","cnm_p105","cnm_075"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":4,"alignmentIds":["alignment:06d5a7e54bf0f6443238260a"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"4.8","reason":"The side is sqrt(3² + 4²) = 5 and the area is 6 × 8 / 2 = 24. Therefore the height is 24 / 5 = 4.8.","status":"matches"},"assessed":true,"bank":"cn-math","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_p147"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"cnm_189_q5","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_075","cnm_p137"],"id":"main","label":"Find the side and divide area by base","methodDirectNodeIds":{"main":["cnm_189","cnm_174","cnm_p147"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_189","cnm_174","cnm_p147","cnm_075","cnm_p137"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":5,"alignmentIds":["alignment:06d5a7e54bf0f6443238260a"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"B, 1/sin(α)","reason":"If b is the horizontal base of the overlap, the perpendicular distance between the slanted boundaries is b sin(α)=1. Therefore its area is b×1=1/sin(α).","status":"matches"},"assessed":true,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_p147"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"1989_AMC_12_Q13","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_p105","cnm_065","cnm_059"],"id":"method1","label":"Find the base using the strip's perpendicular width","methodDirectNodeIds":{"method1":["cnm_p147","cnm_276","cnm_h064"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_p147","cnm_276","cnm_h064","cnm_p105","cnm_065","cnm_059"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":1,"alignmentIds":["alignment:06d5a7e54bf0f6443238260a"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"C: 12 feet","reason":"The crosswalk parallelogram has area 15×40=600. Using a stripe as its base gives 50d=600, so the perpendicular distance is d=12.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_p147"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2001_AMC_10_Q15","reviewStatus":"machine_examined","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"two-parallelogram-heights","label":"Use two base-height pairs","methodDirectNodeIds":{"two-parallelogram-heights":["cnm_p147"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_p147"]},{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_064","cnm_p105"],"id":"two-base-height-pairs","label":"Calculate the same area two ways","methodDirectNodeIds":{"two-base-height-pairs":["cnm_065","cnm_p147"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_065","cnm_p147","cnm_064","cnm_p105"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":3,"alignmentIds":["alignment:06d5a7e54bf0f6443238260a"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"C, 3√3/2","reason":"Because 1+ω+ω²=0, the corner sums are 0 and ±1, ±ω, ±ω². The linear image of the coefficient cube is their convex hull, a regular hexagon of side 1. Its area is 6(√3/4)=3√3/2.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_p147"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2019_AMC_12B_Q24","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"three-rhombi","label":"Three rhombi","methodDirectNodeIds":{"three-rhombi":["cnm_h098","cnm_h101","cnm_p147","cnm_p150"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_h098","cnm_h101","cnm_p147","cnm_p150"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":3,"alignmentIds":["alignment:06d5a7e54bf0f6443238260a"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"C. 40","reason":"In the listed cyclic order, the midpoint parallelogram has horizontal base 5 and height 4, so its area is 20. Joining side midpoints halves a quadrilateral's area, giving rectangle area 2(20)=40.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_p147"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2022_AMC_8_Q18","reviewStatus":"machine_examined","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"midpoint-area-ratio","label":"Midpoint area ratio","methodDirectNodeIds":{"midpoint-area-ratio":["cnm_185","cnm_272","cnm_p147"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_185","cnm_272","cnm_p147"]},{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"official-corner-area","label":"Subtract the four corner-triangle areas","methodDirectNodeIds":{"official-corner-area":["cnm_p147","cnm_p148","cnm_p089","cnm_p150"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_p147","cnm_p148","cnm_p089","cnm_p150"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":4,"alignmentIds":["alignment:06d5a7e54bf0f6443238260a"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"C, 5","reason":"FG is parallel and equal to AB. Triangles EFG and HFG have common base FG, and their heights sum to the distance between AB and CD. Their combined area is half of 10, or 5.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_p147"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"1992_AMC_12_Q24","reviewStatus":"machine_examined","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_183","cnm_p148","cnm_p147"],"id":"shared-base-height-sum","label":"Split along a shared base","methodDirectNodeIds":{"shared-base-height-sum":["cnm_p150","cnm_184"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_p150","cnm_184","cnm_183","cnm_p148","cnm_p147"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":5,"alignmentIds":["alignment:06d5a7e54bf0f6443238260a"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"D (16)","reason":"Writing k=|a-b| gives (c-d)²=18k and (c+d)²=72k. Hence {c,d}={t,3t} and k=2t²/9. Integrality forces 3|t, so c+d≥12 and a+b≥k+2≥4. The tuple (1,3,3,9) attains both bounds, giving 16.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_p147"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2007_AMC_12B_Q20","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"base-times-separation","label":"Parallel-line base and height","methodDirectNodeIds":{"base-times-separation":["cnm_h172","cnm_h173","cnm_h175","cnm_p147"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_h172","cnm_h173","cnm_h175","cnm_p147"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":6,"alignmentIds":["alignment:06d5a7e54bf0f6443238260a"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"A: Art","reason":"The areas for Art, Roger, Paul, and Trisha are (3+5)·3/2=12, 4·2=8, 3·2=6, and 3·4/2=6 square inches. Art's cookies have the largest area, so his batch contains the fewest cookies.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_p147"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2003_AMC_8_Q08","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_p088","cnm_p103"],"id":"m1","label":"Compare cookie areas","methodDirectNodeIds":{"m1":["cnm_p214","cnm_p149","cnm_p089","cnm_p147","cnm_p148"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_p214","cnm_p149","cnm_p089","cnm_p147","cnm_p148","cnm_p088","cnm_p103"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":7,"alignmentIds":["alignment:06d5a7e54bf0f6443238260a"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"C, 9k/8","reason":"Midpoint similarities give QA=AB=BP, hence QP=3AB. Triangles OQP and OCD are similar with side ratio 3, so O is at 3/4 of the parallelogram height h above QP. Therefore [QPO]=(1/2)(3AB)(3h/4)=9k/8.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_p147"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"1974_AMC_12_Q25","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_270","cnm_069","cnm_063","cnm_055","cnm_183","cnm_p147"],"id":"solution:midpoint-similarities:931ddde2192d","label":"Similar triangles and heights","methodDirectNodeIds":{"midpoint-similarities":["cnm_271","cnm_272","cnm_p148"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_271","cnm_272","cnm_p148","cnm_270","cnm_069","cnm_063","cnm_055","cnm_183","cnm_p147"]},{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_082","cnm_089","cnm_055","cnm_183","cnm_p147"],"id":"solution:coordinate-intersections:931ddde2192d","label":"Coordinates with an arbitrary slant","methodDirectNodeIds":{"coordinate-intersections":["cnm_084","cnm_h172","cnm_p148"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_084","cnm_h172","cnm_p148","cnm_082","cnm_089","cnm_055","cnm_183","cnm_p147"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":7,"alignmentIds":["alignment:06d5a7e54bf0f6443238260a"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"D: √3","reason":"ABEF and BCDE are parallelograms because each has a pair of equal parallel opposite sides. Their adjacent sides all have length 1, and each has an included angle of 60°. Each area is 1·sin60°=√3/2, so the total area is √3.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_p147"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"1983_AMC_12_Q04","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_139","cnm_137","cnm_183","cnm_080"],"id":"split-parallelograms","label":"Split the figure into two parallelograms","methodDirectNodeIds":{"split-parallelograms":["cnm_p150","cnm_184","cnm_p147","cnm_174"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_p150","cnm_184","cnm_p147","cnm_174","cnm_139","cnm_137","cnm_183","cnm_080"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":7,"alignmentIds":["alignment:06d5a7e54bf0f6443238260a"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"E. Same area, but the perimeter of I is smaller.","reason":"Taking adjacent grid spacing as 1, I has area 1 and II consists of two triangles of area 1/2 each. Their perimeters are 2+2√2 and 1+2√2+√5, respectively. The second exceeds the first by √5-1>0.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_p147"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2000_AMC_8_Q18","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_p147","cnm_p148","cnm_p105","cnm_064","cnm_053"],"id":"equal-areas-matching-sides","label":"Split the areas and match boundary lengths","methodDirectNodeIds":{"equal-areas-matching-sides":["cnm_p150","cnm_055","cnm_065"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_p150","cnm_055","cnm_065","cnm_p147","cnm_p148","cnm_p105","cnm_064","cnm_053"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":7,"alignmentIds":["alignment:06d5a7e54bf0f6443238260a"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"C: 8","reason":"If the outer side is s, triangle ABD is equilateral, so BD=s, while AC=√3·s. Similarity sends outer AC to inner BD, giving linear scale 1/√3. Splitting the rhombi into corresponding similar triangles gives area scale 1/3, so the inner area is 24/3=8.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_p147"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2006_AMC_10B_Q15","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_110","cnm_268","cnm_p147"],"id":"2006_AMC_10B_Q15_m1","label":"Compare corresponding diagonals","methodDirectNodeIds":{"2006_AMC_10B_Q15_m1":["cnm_189","cnm_139","cnm_174","cnm_270","math:similar-figure-area-scaling"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_189","cnm_139","cnm_174","cnm_270","math:similar-figure-area-scaling","cnm_110","cnm_268","cnm_p147"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":8,"alignmentIds":["alignment:06d5a7e54bf0f6443238260a"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"C: 784","reason":"Write B = (b,b) and D = (d,kd), with b,d positive integers. The area is bd(k - 1), so b·d·(k - 1) = 10^6 = 2^6·5^6. For each prime, its exponent 6 can be distributed among three factors in C(8,2) = 28 ways. These independent choices give 28^2 = 784 distinct parallelograms.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_p147"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2009_AMC_12B_Q22","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["math:prime-factorization","cnm_p147","cnm_174","cnm_083","cnm_183"],"id":"coordinate-area-and-prime-exponents","label":"Convert area into a product of three integers","methodDirectNodeIds":{"coordinate-area-and-prime-exponents":["cnm_084","math:integer-diophantine-equations","cnm_h230","cnm_h231"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_084","math:integer-diophantine-equations","cnm_h230","cnm_h231","math:prime-factorization","cnm_p147","cnm_174","cnm_083","cnm_183"]}]}],"canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_p147"],"l